<main id="main">

<section class="du-hero"><div class="du-hero-l"><p class="du-ey">Heritage outerwear &middot; Est. 1890s</p><h1><span>Duf</span><span>fels</span></h1><p class="du-hero-p">An independent guide to the duffel coat: hooded, toggled, made of heavy wool, and still the warmest way to look relaxed in winter.</p><div class="du-hero-a"><a class="du-btn" href="#toggles">Fasten the toggles</a><a class="du-lnk" href="duffel-coat-guide.html">Read the guide</a></div><div class="du-badge" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><defs><path id="bp" d="M60 60 m-46 0 a46 46 0 1 1 92 0 a46 46 0 1 1 -92 0"/></defs><text><textPath href="#bp">HOOD &#183; TOGGLES &#183; WOOL &#183; ROPE &#183; </textPath></text><rect x="42" y="54" width="36" height="12" rx="6" fill="#B98A56"/></svg></div></div><div class="du-hero-r"><div class="du-hero-i pxw"><img data-px=".12" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1785669430022-12ff54ab8948?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1100&h=1400&q=75" alt="a man in a navy duffel coat and sunglasses leaning on a stone wall" width="1100" height="1400" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></section>

<section class="du-s du-in"><div class="du-w du-in-g"><p class="du-big rv">Four horn toggles, two rope loops, a hood big enough to go over a cap, and wool so dense it stops the wind. The duffel coat is <em>design by necessity</em>.</p><div class="du-in-n stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="4">4</b><span>toggles on a classic front</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="800">800</b><small>g/m&sup2;</small><span>weight of a heavy duffel cloth</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="130">130</b><small>yrs</small><span>of the same honest design</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="du-s du-dk" id="toggles"><div class="du-w du-tg"><div class="du-tg-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 480" class="du-coat" aria-hidden="true"><path class="c-hood" d="M140 70 Q200 10 260 70 L250 110 Q200 85 150 110Z"/><path class="c-body" d="M150 105 L80 140 L60 440 L190 450 L200 130 L210 450 L340 440 L320 140 L250 105 Q200 125 150 105Z"/><path class="c-yoke" d="M80 140 L150 105 Q200 125 250 105 L320 140 L310 175 Q200 160 90 175Z"/><rect class="c-pk" x="95" y="300" width="70" height="80" rx="6"/><rect class="c-pk" x="235" y="300" width="70" height="80" rx="6"/><path class="c-front" id="c-fl" d="M200 130 L190 450"/><path class="c-front" id="c-fr" d="M200 130 L210 450"/><g class="tg" data-i="0"><path class="tg-l" d="M150 150 h40"/><path class="tg-r" d="M250 150 h-40"/><rect class="tg-b" x="170" y="143" width="40" height="13" rx="6.5"/></g><g class="tg" data-i="1"><path class="tg-l" d="M150 215 h40"/><path class="tg-r" d="M250 215 h-40"/><rect class="tg-b" x="170" y="208" width="40" height="13" rx="6.5"/></g><g class="tg" data-i="2"><path class="tg-l" d="M150 280 h40"/><path class="tg-r" d="M250 280 h-40"/><rect class="tg-b" x="170" y="273" width="40" height="13" rx="6.5"/></g><g class="tg" data-i="3"><path class="tg-l" d="M150 345 h40"/><path class="tg-r" d="M250 345 h-40"/><rect class="tg-b" x="170" y="338" width="40" height="13" rx="6.5"/></g></svg></div><div><p class="du-ey">Interactive</p><h2 class="rv">Fasten it, one toggle at a time</h2><p class="du-p">Duffel toggles were designed for gloved hands. Tap a toggle to loop it through its rope, or fasten them all.</p><div class="du-tg-b"><button type="button" class="du-btn" id="tg-all">Fasten all</button><button type="button" class="du-btn du-btn2" id="tg-none">Open coat</button></div><p class="du-tg-o" id="tg-o" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="du-tg-ph rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768016288075-5f9dcf7759f0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=460&q=75" alt="a man in a grey toggle coat leaning against a lamppost in falling snow" width="760" height="460" loading="lazy"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="du-s du-tl"><div class="du-w"><div class="du-cen"><p class="du-ey">A short history</p><h2 class="rv">From Flemish cloth to everyone&rsquo;s coat</h2></div><div class="du-tl-w"><div class="du-tl-line"><i id="tl-fill"></i></div><div class="du-tl-r"><div class="du-tl-y"><b>1890s</b></div><div class="du-tl-c rv"><div class="du-tl-i rv-w"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1697811614091-426210be3695?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=480&q=75" alt="a man in a heavy coat in black and white" width="640" height="480" loading="lazy"></div><h3>The cloth</h3><p>A thick, napped woollen cloth from the town of Duffel, near Antwerp, gives the coat its name.</p></div></div><div class="du-tl-r"><div class="du-tl-y"><b>1940s</b></div><div class="du-tl-c rv"><div class="du-tl-i rv-w"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581337204900-aa4e6020759c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=480&q=75" alt="a man in a brown coat and plaid scarf" width="640" height="480" loading="lazy"></div><h3>The sea</h3><p>Navies issue hooded, toggle-fastened coats in heavy wool: easy to close with gloved hands on a cold deck.</p></div></div><div class="du-tl-r"><div class="du-tl-y"><b>1950s</b></div><div class="du-tl-c rv"><div class="du-tl-i rv-w"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542753867-1d566cec81ac?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=480&q=75" alt="a smiling woman in a hooded winter coat in low sun" width="640" height="480" loading="lazy"></div><h3>The campus</h3><p>Surplus coats find their way to students, artists and writers, and the duffel becomes a civilian classic.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="du-s du-fit" id="fit"><div class="du-w du-fit-g"><div><p class="du-ey">Fit finder</p><h2 class="rv">The right size, with room for a jumper</h2><p class="du-p">A duffel is worn over layers. Tell us your chest and what you wear beneath, and pick a length.</p><label class="du-lab" for="ft-c">Chest measurement <output id="ft-cv">100 cm</output><input type="range" id="ft-c" min="80" max="130" value="100"></label><fieldset class="du-fs"><legend>Underneath</legend><div class="du-chips"><label><input type="radio" name="ly" value="4" checked><span>Shirt</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ly" value="8"><span>Fine knit</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ly" value="12"><span>Chunky knit</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="du-fs"><legend>Length</legend><div class="du-chips"><label><input type="radio" name="ln" value="0"><span>Hip</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ln" value="1" checked><span>Thigh</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ln" value="2"><span>Knee</span></label></div></fieldset></div><div class="du-fit-o"><div class="du-fit-fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 300" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="80" cy="34" r="20" class="fg"/><path d="M50 62h60l12 120H38z" class="fg"/><path d="M48 190h26l-2 100H54zM86 190h26l-6 100H90z" class="fg"/><rect id="ft-coat" x="34" y="60" width="92" height="150" rx="12" class="fc"/></svg></div><div><p class="du-ey">Your coat</p><b class="du-fit-b" id="ft-o">108 cm</b><p id="ft-t"></p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="du-s du-lks"><div class="du-w du-lks-h"><div><p class="du-ey">Colour edit</p><h2 class="rv">Four shades of the same coat</h2></div><p class="du-hint">Drag &rarr;</p></div><div class="hs du-hs"><div class="du-lk"><div class="du-lk-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579104734852-84455dde242e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="a person in a grey and blue wool coat" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="du-lk-t"><span>01</span><h3>Charcoal</h3><p>Sharp in town, endlessly practical.</p></div></div><div class="du-lk"><div class="du-lk-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565532070333-43edd7d75c90?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="a yellow coat hanging on a hook" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="du-lk-t"><span>02</span><h3>Mustard</h3><p>A cheerful colour for grey days.</p></div></div><div class="du-lk"><div class="du-lk-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1715536369803-435f657151a3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="a man in a dark coat looking at his phone" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="du-lk-t"><span>03</span><h3>Navy</h3><p>The naval original, with everything.</p></div></div><div class="du-lk"><div class="du-lk-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1755214832310-074c4cc45372?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="close-up of grey wool fabric tied in a knot" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="du-lk-t"><span>04</span><h3>Grey melton</h3><p>Dense cloth that shrugs off wind.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="du-gl"><div class="du-w du-gl-g"><a class="du-gl-a rv" href="duffel-coat-guide.html"><span>Guide one</span><b>The Duffel Coat</b><em>History, features and cloth: what makes a duffel a duffel.</em><i>Read the guide</i></a><a class="du-gl-a rv" href="duffel-fit-care-guide.html"><span>Guide two</span><b>Fit &amp; Care</b><em>Choosing the size and length, and keeping heavy wool looking good.</em><i>Read the guide</i></a></div></section>

